<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Otto the Child</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1204">1204</a>–<a href="/years/1252">1252</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/13th-century">13th century</a> · Also known as Otto I, Duke of Brunswick-Lüneburg</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Otto the Child was a grandson of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/henry-the-lion">Henry the Lion</a> and the first duke of Brunswick-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/luneburg">Lüneburg</a>. At the Diet of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mainz">Mainz</a> in 1235 he surrendered his family's lands to Emperor Frederick II and received them back as a duchy, reconciling the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/house-of-welf">Guelphs</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hohenstaufen">Hohenstaufen</a>. His sons divided the duchy in 1269.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/otto-the-child.jpg" alt="Otto the Child" width="320" height="512" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hans Bornemann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:FriedrichIIbelehntottodaskind.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
